Paint the default indicator on the default button only

drawPrimitiveButton() treats a button as the default button when three
conditions hold. The button effect is not plain, the mouse-over colour is
glow, and the focus style is full or filled. Every focused button of such
a configuration then takes the default button colours, the darkened fill,
the coloured border, the corner mark or the glow. The button that the
style option reports as the default button loses its own mark, because
each neighbour now carries the same mark. The Default Button page of the
dialog names the one button that takes the mark.

The label of a promoted button stays plain, because drawControl() reads
the DefaultButton feature of the style option for the bold font. The
promotion therefore contradicts the style option that it overrides.

The style now takes the default flag from the style option alone. A
focused button keeps the rectangle of its focus style, which the focus
option draws.

The change sits on the branch work/style-paint of the local tree, as commit 2 of 21.
A new merge request on system/qtcurve takes that branch.

Drop this patch when upstream merges the change.

